# ── Secrets & environment ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── Local config (template + local copy, same pattern as .env) ───────────────
/config.yaml
!/config.example.yaml

# ── The workspace: the ONE output root — everything the engine writes ────────
workspace/

# ── Legacy (pre-workspace) runtime state; kept for un-migrated checkouts ─────
data_lake/
reports/
state/
/MEMORY.md
*.parquet
*.db

# ── Legacy strategy tier layout (pre-workspace); kept one release as protection ──
# The tiers now live under workspace/ (covered above). These lines only protect a
# checkout whose un-migrated __tmp/ and champions/ still sit beside the seeds.
strategies/__tmp/
strategies/champions/

# ── Operator mandate: ship only the scaffold; personal input stays local ─────
# The repo carries the template (MANDATE.md.example), the five shipped profiles, tune-first,
# the README, and one reference example. An operator's own MANDATE.md, custom personalities
# (mandate/<name>.md, profiles/<name>.md), and personal references are gitignored so editing
# a mandate never pollutes the repo. Add a NEW shipped profile? re-include it below.
mandate/*.md
!mandate/README.md
!mandate/tune-first.md
mandate/profiles/*.md
!mandate/profiles/aggressive.md
!mandate/profiles/conservative.md
!mandate/profiles/long-term.md
!mandate/profiles/short-term.md
!mandate/profiles/sector-specialist.md
mandate/references/*
!mandate/references/.gitkeep
!mandate/references/example-watchlist.md
!mandate/references/high-vol-momentum-brief.md

# ── Benchmark cases: ship the scaffold; a mined corpus stays the operator's ──
# The repo carries cases/README.md (the case file format) and nothing else. Every case
# under cases/<site_id>/ is local: a mined corpus is harvested from an operator's own runs
# and carries their briefs, symbols and run ids. Shipping a REVIEWED corpus to every user?
# re-include it below by name, one line per directory — an explicit act, never a default.
cases/*
!cases/README.md
# The coder corpus (#218) is the first reviewed one: its README and its two CURATED buckets
# ship to every user, while the two HARVESTED buckets stay local — cases/coder/field/ and
# cases/coder/replay/ carry an operator's own briefs, symbols and run ids, and are covered by
# the deny-by-default 'cases/coder/*' below rather than named. A loose case beside the buckets
# is ignored too, so filing one wrongly leaks nothing.
!cases/coder/
cases/coder/*
!cases/coder/README.md
!cases/coder/edge/
!cases/coder/canary/

